{
  "id": "Compound::DB00180 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Flunisolide is implicated in the pathogenesis of Candida Albicans Infection through a chain of interactions involving therapeutic glucocorticoids. The evidence suggests that Flunisolide, through its role in causing infections, is linked to Cyp3a4 via binding interactions with various glucocorticoids, including Fluticasone Furoate, Triamcinolone, and Ciclesonide. These glucocorticoids, in turn, bind to Cyp3a4, a key enzyme involved in steroid metabolism. The shared ancestry of these compounds with therapeutic glucocorticoids and their common pathway to Cyp3a4 underscores a mechanistic link between Flunisolide and Cyp3a4. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cyp3a4 in the metabolic processing of glucocorticoids, which may influence the pharmacological effects of these compounds. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Flunisolide and Cyp3a4 through the intermediation of glucocorticoid binding, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Flunisolide may modulate Cyp3a4 activity.",
